<main>
    <div class="roadmap-header fade-up fade-up-1">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="dates">Last updated 2026-07-03 &middot; plain-language beta privacy policy &mdash; a lawyer hasn't blessed these yet</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p>Parachute exists so your thoughts have a private place to live. That only works if you can trust what happens to them. This page says, plainly, what <strong>Open Parachute, PBC</strong> (a Colorado Public Benefit Corporation) stores and what we will never do with it. Questions to <a href="mailto:hello@parachute.computer">hello@parachute.computer</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Your email address</strong> &mdash; it's how you sign in (magic links) and how we reach you.</li>
            <li><strong>The notes you write</strong> &mdash; your vault's contents, stored so we can show them back to you and back them up. We don't read them except when you explicitly ask us to help debug something, or when the law compels us.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage metrics</strong> &mdash; basics like storage used, when your vault was last active, and anonymous page analytics on this website (cookieless). Enough to run the service and see what's working; no tracking you around the web.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>We don't sell your data.</strong> Not to advertisers, not to brokers, not to anyone. Our business is you paying us for a service, full stop.</li>
            <li><strong>We don't train AI on your vault.</strong> Your notes are yours. When <em>you</em> connect an AI to your vault, that's your choice and your AI &mdash; we don't feed your notes to models on our side.</li>
            <li><strong>We don't run ads</strong> and we don't use advertising trackers.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Who else touches the data (subprocessors)</h2>
        <p>We keep the list short:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; hosts the service and stores vault data and backups on our behalf.</li>
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> &mdash; will process payments when paid plans land. Stripe sees your payment details; we never store your card number.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If this list grows, we'll update this page before the new subprocessor handles your data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Email we send</h2>
        <p>Signing in works by <strong>magic link</strong>, so you'll get an email each time you sign in &mdash; that one's unavoidable. Beyond that, new accounts get a short <strong>three-email onboarding series</strong> (a welcome, a "connect your AI?" nudge, and a feedback ask), and we may occasionally send service announcements that affect your account. Every non-essential email has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing is honored immediately. No marketing lists, no partner emails.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>Delete your vault or your account and the data goes with it, including from our backups as they age out (backups are kept for a bounded window for disaster recovery). Want everything gone, or a copy of everything we hold about you? Email <a href="mailto:hello@parachute.computer">hello@parachute.computer</a> and we'll do it &mdash; no forms, no retention tricks. And you can <a href="/terms/">export everything yourself</a> at any time, no permission needed.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date at the top and email registered users before the change takes effect. See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    </section>
</main>
